db/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7487ada-70fd-5ba0-8873-b0b458efd67c" :question/math-academy-id "q-183348" :question/problem "$\\,$ If $x$ has more than three divisors, then $x$ is composite.\n\nWhich of the following is logically equivalent to the conditional predicate above?" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote by $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ has more than three divisors.\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is composite.\n\nThen, our initial sentence can be written as $P(x)⇒Q(x),$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬P(x)∨Q(x).\n$$\n\nThe negation of $P(x)$ can be written as\n\n- $¬P(x):$ $x$ doesn't have more than three divisors.\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ doesn't have more than three divisors, or $x$ is composite."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407606 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198261 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6db336-845a-506a-b020-cced1b38e23a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Implications and Equivalences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3da861c8-066a-5c61-b09e-b19fe4847a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407577} {:answer/id #uuid "55d4b454-b90c-53f1-bb03-1433437d6223" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407580} {:answer/id #uuid "7d2e08a4-12e2-56a6-afe0-aaec4835514d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407585} {:answer/id #uuid "9b88c49e-083d-575c-8a5a-f1c566cae7ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407588} {:answer/id #uuid "b06266a6-9eff-553d-bee6-4acee85a7d2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3da861c8-066a-5c61-b09e-b19fe4847a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407577} :answer-field/id #uuid "219bccf4-7364-5184-b837-9a47fc6fccc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407598}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "db5f04ef-3cc1-58de-87ac-cce7945d8e35" :question/math-academy-id "q-183355" :question/problem "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $x\\in Z.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $-x\\in Z.$\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)⇔B(x)?$\n\n- If $x\\in Z$ then $-x\\in Z$, and if $-x\\in Z$ then $x\\in Z.$\n- $x\\in Z$ is equivalent to $-x\\in Z.$\n- $x\\in Z$ if and only if $-x\\in Z.$" :question/worked-solution "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $x\\in Z$ if and only if $-x\\in Z.$\n\n- $x\\in Z$ is equivalent to $-x\\in Z.$\n\n- If $x\\in Z$ then $-x\\in Z$, and if $-x\\in Z$ then $x\\in Z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381679 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198261 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6db336-845a-506a-b020-cced1b38e23a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Implications and Equivalences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24f5e0da-6ff9-54f8-9899-0fcb4faf174b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381681} {:answer/id #uuid "6ba148f2-8aed-5afe-b8f6-2d6df1077df1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381682} {:answer/id #uuid "2514634f-1c9a-516d-9f01-6fcf8e8bb2ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381683} {:answer/id #uuid "eb6bb8e3-7838-5de4-b233-6ca16778703e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381684} {:answer/id #uuid "d12b87f7-5b3d-5c51-b825-9978e6d5f710" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2514634f-1c9a-516d-9f01-6fcf8e8bb2ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381683} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8661f64-c8fd-5a5e-8d68-13ad71e9e23d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9aa776da-0143-5b4b-9d08-2751ea2726a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-183357" :question/problem "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $3\\,|\\,x.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $3\\,|\\,(x+15).$\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)⇔B(x)?$\n\n- $3\\,|\\,x$ if and only if $5\\,|x.$\n- If $3\\,|\\,x$ then $3\\,|\\,(x+15),$ or if $3\\,|\\,(x+15)$ then $3\\,|\\,x.$\n- If $3\\,|\\,x$ then $3\\,|\\,(x+15),$ and if $3\\,|\\,(x+15)$ then $3\\,|\\,x.$" :question/worked-solution "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $3\\,|\\,x$ if and only if $3\\,|\\,(x+15).$\n\n- $3\\,|\\,x$ is equivalent to $3\\,|\\,(x+15).$\n\n- If $3\\,|\\,x$ then $3\\,|\\,(x+15),$ and if $3\\,|\\,(x+15)$ then $3\\,|\\,x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381686 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198260 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c5f2a86-209a-5bb3-a3f2-77d679adb0a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of an Equivalence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95fc19e3-8ca8-5969-9f04-b5b491957e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/01/01776646145493da01e17a764ee1b71161595bcc249f376fc18cd9325a8218e7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381688} {:answer/id #uuid "86cdb6bc-b584-57f3-9dbb-3aaf9f6680e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e4/e43b58f0eb6ca96a0d9849b75b3d72e3100671405ebe6196588cc482acd2cb9d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381689} {:answer/id #uuid "af129731-17cf-5410-9081-c5e4ee3cd395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c8/c8b297d8b299fd2ed1c6e82fc8513de2cf30f4b4ad148e4c15d53941c7c40d62.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381690} {:answer/id #uuid "daa7f005-3d69-5915-b55a-e2ecdf47ba3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b8/b879f723061d5565f47bc076a85ab43a91f6981e867d2339061339a771f5043d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381691} {:answer/id #uuid "a3f2c811-72b8-53eb-915c-67d6bafee544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d2/d241c79ec2ab5c8ddc6cc4d1cf33f3355a91c44b30661afcf90e39e1b8ff6969.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95fc19e3-8ca8-5969-9f04-b5b491957e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/01/01776646145493da01e17a764ee1b71161595bcc249f376fc18cd9325a8218e7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381688} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f00ecb4-5a2c-5bd4-86e6-6fc0f7553e8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "96ab9b12-c6bc-56bd-aeba-ea72894263c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-183383" :question/problem "![](images/17/17a493e38294911702a94b8755111db85e7445f03d4d149602b57eebf009f14b.png)\n\nThe shaded regions above represent the truth sets of predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ defined over the universal set ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following is the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have that \n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇔Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we sketch the set ${T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}:$\n\n![](images/e9/e995ce9652d431c39c7a629a5e825c91fcdb2da56b83ad371c6bb319bc548eb9.png)\n\nThen, we sketch the set ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}$ and ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}:$\n\n![](images/fa/fa491500bff1c1e9d0f8453552f33b8deed066e3799a36817d039fc625eee47d.png)\n\nAs a result, ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}$ is the following: \n\n![](images/fb/fbcbb5ebd87fef90163ce5a358beb7bc40b4c4b3d91b89684500577ccedf2b13.png)\n\nFinally, to get the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x),$ we take all the points that belong to ${T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}$ or ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}:$\n\n![](images/01/01776646145493da01e17a764ee1b71161595bcc249f376fc18cd9325a8218e7.png)"}]}
